 # RadSplat
-
-
 ## Overview
-RadSplat is a method for initializing 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) representations by leveraging the robust geometric priors of a trained Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of poor initialization quality and topological inconsistencies inherent in raw Structure-from-Motion (SfM) point clouds [S1, unofficial]. By converting a dense NeRF-derived point cloud into Gaussians, it achieves high-quality rendering with unprecedented speed (900+ FPS) while circumventing the need for extensive per-scene gradient descent loops [S1, unofficial].
+RadSplat initializes 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) by converting a dense point cloud derived from a trained Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) into Gaussians [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the topological inconsistencies and sparsity of raw Structure-from-Motion (SfM) point clouds [S1, unofficial]. The method bypasses or drastically shortens the per-scene gradient descent loop required by standard 3DGS [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-RadSplat operates as a hybrid initialization and pruning strategy. It bypasses the standard SfM-based initialization and subsequent long optimization phases by using a pre-trained NeRF to generate a dense, accurate point cloud, which is then converted into 3D Gaussians [S1, S2, unofficial].
-
-**Inputs:**
-*   A trained NeRF model for the target scene.
-*   Sparse multi-view images (used to train the initial NeRF, though the NeRF itself is the direct input for Gaussian generation).
-
-**Outputs:**
-*   A set of $N$ 3D Gaussians $\{G_i\}_{i=1}^N$ with optimized position, rotation, scale, opacity, and appearance parameters.
-
-**Data Structures:**
-The output is a standard 3DGS primitive list. Each primitive $i$ contains:
-*   Position $\mathbf{p}_i \in \mathbb{R}^3$
-*   Rotation $q_i \in \mathbb{R}^4$ (unit quaternion)
-*   Scale $\mathbf{s}_i \in \mathbb{R}^3$
-*   Opacity $\alpha_i \in [0, 1]$
-*   Appearance parameters (e.g., spherical harmonic coefficients)
-
