 ## Background
-RadSplat was introduced as a method to improve the initialization of 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1, S2, unofficial]. It addresses the limitations of raw SfM initialization, which often suffers from noise and topological errors [S1, unofficial]. The method is cited in surveys on 3D Gaussian Splatting rasterization and recent advances in the field [S1, S2, unofficial].
